claimed: chunk-flush — make chunked merging safe on slow/unending sources: (a) Flush as a real operation in the row, which the chunker interprets by emitting whatever it holds, so a producer can mark a boundary (end of an LLM message, end of a frame); (b) an optional time-based flush as a merge parameter, so a partial chunk cannot wait forever. Hazard to avoid: Async.timeout CANCELS the loser, and cancelling an in-flight uncons on a live source can lose an element -- so the timer must not race the pull. Shape: buffer in a TRef, a flusher fiber taking what has accumulated (one uncontended CAS per element), never touching the pull. Measure the cost against merge(chunked=true).
